    <programlisting>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">#<sp/>Network<sp/>Dynamics<sp/>{#nd}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">This<sp/>page<sp/>is<sp/>dedicated<sp/>to<sp/>terminology<sp/>pertaining<sp/>to<sp/>&quot;network<sp/>dynamics&quot;<sp/>in<sp/>general,<sp/>as<sp/>well<sp/>as<sp/>how<sp/>certain<sp/>concepts<sp/>are<sp/>implemented/interpreted<sp/>in<sp/>NDXL.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">##<sp/>What<sp/>is<sp/>Meant<sp/>by<sp/>&quot;State<sp/>Vector&quot;?<sp/>{#state-vector}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">An<sp/>agent&apos;s<sp/>state<sp/>vector<sp/>is<sp/>the<sp/>vector<sp/>of<sp/>time-dependent<sp/>properties<sp/>that<sp/>fully<sp/>describe<sp/>the<sp/>agent.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">Because<sp/>a<sp/>scalar<sp/>can<sp/>be<sp/>represented<sp/>as<sp/>a<sp/>unit-length<sp/>array,<sp/>NDXL<sp/>treats<sp/>all<sp/>state<sp/>vectors<sp/>as<sp/>arrays,<sp/>allowing<sp/>for<sp/>multidimensional<sp/>dynamics<sp/>to<sp/>be<sp/>evaluated<sp/>by<sp/>default:<sp/>the<sp/>time<sp/>derivative<sp/>for<sp/>each<sp/>element<sp/>is<sp/>just<sp/>written<sp/>in-place<sp/>to<sp/>the<sp/>output<sp/>array<sp/>similar<sp/>to<sp/>the<sp/>@ref<sp/>examples<sp/>&quot;Getting<sp/>Started&quot;<sp/>example.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">In<sp/>a<sp/>power<sp/>grid<sp/>modelled<sp/>by<sp/>the<sp/>swing<sp/>equation,<sp/>for<sp/>example,<sp/>each<sp/>node<sp/>has<sp/>two<sp/>states,<sp/>namely,<sp/>its<sp/>phase<sp/>angle<sp/>\f$\theta\f$<sp/>and<sp/>frequency<sp/>\f$\omega\f$,<sp/>while<sp/>each<sp/>transmission<sp/>line<sp/>is<sp/>typically<sp/>only<sp/>described<sp/>by<sp/>its<sp/>coupling<sp/>constant<sp/>\f$A\f$.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">We<sp/>can<sp/>explicitly<sp/>write<sp/>the<sp/>state<sp/>vector<sp/>of<sp/>node<sp/>\f$i\f$<sp/>as:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">\f[</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>\vec{x}_i<sp/>=<sp/>\left\langle\theta_i,~\omega_i\right\rangle</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">\f]</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">And<sp/>similarly<sp/>the<sp/>state<sp/>vector<sp/>of<sp/>edge<sp/>\f$ij\f$<sp/>is:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">\f[</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>\vec{y}_{ij}<sp/>=<sp/>\left\langle<sp/>A_{ij}\right\rangle</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">\f]</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">###<sp/>Do<sp/>all<sp/>elements<sp/>of<sp/>a<sp/>state<sp/>vector<sp/>change<sp/>over<sp/>time?</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">They<sp/>can,<sp/>but<sp/>they<sp/>do<sp/>not<sp/>necessarily<sp/>have<sp/>to.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">An<sp/>element<sp/>constant<sp/>with<sp/>respect<sp/>to<sp/>time<sp/>is<sp/>called<sp/>a<sp/>&lt;b&gt;static<sp/>element&lt;/b&gt;,<sp/>and<sp/>if<sp/>all<sp/>elements<sp/>of<sp/>an<sp/>agent&apos;s<sp/>state<sp/>vector<sp/>are<sp/>static,<sp/>then<sp/>the<sp/>agent<sp/>itself<sp/>is<sp/>said<sp/>to<sp/>be<sp/>a<sp/>&lt;b&gt;static<sp/>agent&lt;/b&gt;.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">Static<sp/>elements<sp/>in<sp/>NDXL<sp/>are<sp/>characterised<sp/>by<sp/>a<sp/>return<sp/>value<sp/>of<sp/>\f$0\f$<sp/>for<sp/>that<sp/>element<sp/>in<sp/>its<sp/>dynamics<sp/>function;<sp/>static<sp/>agents<sp/>can<sp/>be<sp/>simply<sp/>assinged<sp/>`NULL`<sp/>for<sp/>their<sp/>dynamics.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">###<sp/>What<sp/>if<sp/>agent<sp/>dynamics<sp/>depend<sp/>on<sp/>constants<sp/>in<sp/>the<sp/>equation?<sp/>{#dynamicsexample}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">Suppose<sp/>the<sp/>dynamics<sp/>of<sp/>a<sp/>vertex<sp/>are<sp/>given<sp/>by</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">\f[</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>\frac{d\vec{x}}{dt}<sp/>=<sp/>Ct<sp/>+<sp/>D\vec{x}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">\f]</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">where<sp/>\f$C\f$<sp/>and<sp/>\f$D\f$<sp/>are<sp/>constants.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">In<sp/>the<sp/>agent&apos;s<sp/>constructor,<sp/>these<sp/>numbers<sp/>are<sp/>passed<sp/>using<sp/>the<sp/>`void*<sp/>params`<sp/>argument,<sp/>which<sp/>is<sp/>always<sp/>the<sp/>last<sp/>argument<sp/>in<sp/>a<sp/>constructor.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">During<sp/>dynamics<sp/>evaluation,<sp/>they<sp/>can<sp/>be<sp/>extracted<sp/>by<sp/>converting<sp/>the<sp/>`void*<sp/>params`<sp/>to<sp/>whatever<sp/>datatype<sp/>the<sp/>constants<sp/>initially<sp/>were<sp/>defined<sp/>as,<sp/>as<sp/>shown<sp/>in<sp/>the<sp/>@ref<sp/>examples<sp/>&quot;Getting<sp/>Started&quot;<sp/>example.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">##<sp/>Heterogeneous<sp/>Dynamics<sp/>{#hetero-dynamics}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">It<sp/>is<sp/>common<sp/>to<sp/>express<sp/>the<sp/>dynamics<sp/>of<sp/>network<sp/>agents<sp/>as<sp/>a<sp/>single<sp/>function<sp/>according<sp/>to<sp/>which<sp/>each<sp/>agent&apos;s<sp/>state<sp/>vector<sp/>evolves,<sp/>and<sp/>have<sp/>their<sp/>state<sp/>vectors<sp/>and<sp/>`void*<sp/>params`<sp/>refer<sp/>to<sp/>parameters.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">In<sp/>the<sp/>Kuramoto<sp/>model,<sp/>for<sp/>example,<sp/>each<sp/>vertex<sp/>has<sp/>a<sp/>unit<sp/>state<sp/>vector<sp/>containing<sp/>its<sp/>phase<sp/>\f$\theta\f$,<sp/>with<sp/>its<sp/>`void*<sp/>params`<sp/>containing<sp/>its<sp/>eigenfrequency,<sp/>and<sp/>evolves<sp/>according<sp/>to<sp/>the<sp/>agentic<sp/>Kuramoto<sp/>model.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">In<sp/>the<sp/>swing<sp/>equation,<sp/>each<sp/>vertex<sp/>has<sp/>a<sp/>two-component<sp/>state<sp/>vector<sp/>containing<sp/>its<sp/>phase<sp/>\f$\theta\f$<sp/>and<sp/>frequency<sp/>\f$\omega\f$,<sp/>and<sp/>evolves<sp/>according<sp/>to<sp/>the<sp/>swing<sp/>equation.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">There<sp/>is,<sp/>however,<sp/>no<sp/>strict<sp/>requirement<sp/>saying<sp/>agents<sp/>must:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">-<sp/>Have<sp/>identically<sp/>cardinal<sp/>state<sp/>vectors</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">-<sp/>Depend<sp/>on<sp/>the<sp/>same<sp/>time-variant<sp/>parameters<sp/>as<sp/>others</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">-<sp/>Evolve<sp/>according<sp/>to<sp/>the<sp/>same<sp/>dynamics,<sp/>noise,<sp/>or<sp/>discrete<sp/>callback<sp/>functions</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">-<sp/>Be<sp/>influenced<sp/>by<sp/>the<sp/>same<sp/>noise<sp/>channels<sp/>and/or<sp/>to<sp/>the<sp/>same<sp/>degree</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">-<sp/>Share<sp/>user-defined<sp/>`void*<sp/>params`<sp/>(constants)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">-<sp/>Have<sp/>the<sp/>same<sp/>initial<sp/>conditions</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">Whenever<sp/>one<sp/>or<sp/>more<sp/>of<sp/>the<sp/>first<sp/>four<sp/>conditions<sp/>is<sp/>false,<sp/>the<sp/>agents<sp/>are<sp/>said<sp/>to<sp/>be<sp/>heterogeneous<sp/>(initial<sp/>conditions<sp/>and<sp/>constants<sp/>are<sp/>usually<sp/>unique<sp/>by<sp/>default).</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">This<sp/>gives<sp/>rise<sp/>to<sp/>the<sp/>term<sp/>&quot;heterogeneous<sp/>dynamics&quot;,<sp/>simply<sp/>meaning<sp/>that<sp/>two<sp/>or<sp/>more<sp/>agents<sp/>in<sp/>the<sp/>network<sp/>do<sp/>not<sp/>exhibit<sp/>common<sp/>dynamics.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">This<sp/>can<sp/>be,<sp/>for<sp/>example:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">-<sp/>One<sp/>node<sp/>evolving<sp/>according<sp/>to<sp/>the<sp/>Kuramoto<sp/>model,<sp/>its<sp/>neighbour<sp/>to<sp/>the<sp/>swing<sp/>equation</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">-<sp/>One<sp/>node<sp/>being<sp/>static,<sp/>its<sp/>neighbour<sp/>dynamic</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">-<sp/>One<sp/>node<sp/>being<sp/>@ref<sp/>stochasticity<sp/>&quot;stochastic&quot;,<sp/>its<sp/>neighbour<sp/>purely<sp/>deterministic</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">-<sp/>One<sp/>node<sp/>having<sp/>a<sp/>ten-element<sp/>state<sp/>vector,<sp/>its<sp/>neighbour<sp/>a<sp/>scalar<sp/>state</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">-<sp/>One<sp/>node<sp/>being<sp/>influenced<sp/>by<sp/>noise<sp/>channels<sp/>\f$1\f$,<sp/>\f$3\f$,<sp/>and<sp/>\f$6\f$,<sp/>its<sp/>neighbour<sp/>by<sp/>channels<sp/>\f$2\f$<sp/>and<sp/>\f$5\f$</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">NDXL<sp/>makes<sp/>simulating<sp/>heterogeneous<sp/>dynamics<sp/>easy<sp/>by<sp/>assigning<sp/>agent<sp/>properties<sp/>directly<sp/>to<sp/>the<sp/>agents<sp/>themselves,<sp/>as<sp/>outlined<sp/>in<sp/>the<sp/>@ref<sp/>hetero<sp/>&quot;Heterogeneous<sp/>Dynamics&quot;<sp/>example.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">##<sp/>Stochasticity<sp/>{#stochasticity}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">The<sp/>default<sp/>network<sp/>dynamics<sp/>equations<sp/>are<sp/>written<sp/>as<sp/>purely<sp/>deterministic<sp/>ODEs,<sp/>however,<sp/>some<sp/>systems<sp/>exhibit<sp/>random<sp/>fluctuations<sp/>in<sp/>the<sp/>differential<sp/>equation<sp/>signal.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">These<sp/>fluctuations<sp/>are<sp/>called<sp/>noise,<sp/>and<sp/>add<sp/>an<sp/>element<sp/>of<sp/>stochasticity<sp/>to<sp/>the<sp/>system,<sp/>transforming<sp/>the<sp/>governing<sp/>dynamics<sp/>from<sp/>an<sp/>ODE<sp/>to<sp/>an<sp/>SDE<sp/>(stochastic<sp/>differential<sp/>equation).</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">The<sp/>stochastic<sp/>contributions<sp/>are<sp/>assumed<sp/>to<sp/>follow<sp/>Brownian<sp/>motion,<sp/>and<sp/>the<sp/>random<sp/>path<sp/>taken<sp/>from<sp/>start<sp/>to<sp/>finish<sp/>is<sp/>called<sp/>a<sp/>Wiener<sp/>process.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">This<sp/>process<sp/>is<sp/>further<sp/>documented<sp/>in<sp/>the<sp/>@ref<sp/>sde<sp/>&quot;Stochasticity&quot;<sp/>examples.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">##<sp/>Delays<sp/>{#delays}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">A<sp/>delay<sp/>is<sp/>a<sp/>concept<sp/>in<sp/>information<sp/>theory<sp/>that<sp/>pertains<sp/>to<sp/>the<sp/>time<sp/>\f$\tau\f$<sp/>taken<sp/>for<sp/>information<sp/>to<sp/>travel<sp/>from<sp/>point<sp/>A<sp/>to<sp/>point<sp/>B.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">In<sp/>the<sp/>context<sp/>of<sp/>network<sp/>dynamics,<sp/>and<sp/>specifically<sp/>under<sp/>the<sp/>physical<sp/>interpretation<sp/>of<sp/>a<sp/>network,<sp/>&quot;delays&quot;<sp/>refer<sp/>to<sp/>the<sp/>time<sp/>taken<sp/>for<sp/>a<sp/>signal<sp/>to<sp/>propagate<sp/>from<sp/>one<sp/>vertex<sp/>to<sp/>its<sp/>neighbour<sp/>along<sp/>a<sp/>given<sp/>edge.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">NDXL<sp/>therefore<sp/>treats<sp/>delays<sp/>as<sp/>explicit<sp/>edge<sp/>properties,<sp/>and<sp/>each<sp/>edge<sp/>is<sp/>responsible<sp/>for<sp/>mediating<sp/>delayed<sp/>interactions<sp/>between<sp/>the<sp/>vertices<sp/>it<sp/>connects.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">The<sp/>memory<sp/>and<sp/>implications<sp/>are<sp/>documented<sp/>in<sp/>@ref<sp/>edge_creation<sp/>&quot;edge<sp/>creation&quot;,<sp/>while<sp/>the<sp/>mathematical<sp/>details<sp/>are<sp/>further<sp/>explained<sp/>in<sp/>the<sp/>@ref<sp/>dde<sp/>&quot;Delays&quot;<sp/>examples.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">##<sp/>Higher-Order<sp/>Dynamics<sp/>{#higherorder}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">The<sp/>descriptions<sp/>of<sp/>differential<sp/>equations<sp/>governing<sp/>agent<sp/>dynamics<sp/>have<sp/>thus<sp/>far<sp/>(@ref<sp/>dynamicsexample<sp/>&quot;Dynamics&quot;<sp/>and<sp/>@ref<sp/>stochasticity)<sp/>been<sp/>of<sp/>first-order:<sp/>\f$\frac{d\vec{x}}{dt}\f$.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">Of<sp/>course,<sp/>many<sp/>systems<sp/>exhibit<sp/>higher-order<sp/>dynamics,<sp/>written<sp/>as<sp/>\f$\frac{d^n\vec{x}}{dt^n}\f$.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">To<sp/>solve<sp/>these<sp/>systems<sp/>using<sp/>the<sp/>first-order<sp/>solvers,<sp/>we<sp/>must<sp/>rewrite<sp/>the<sp/>\f$n^{th}\f$-order<sp/>equation<sp/>as<sp/>a<sp/>set<sp/>of<sp/>\f$n\f$<sp/>coupled<sp/>first-order<sp/>equations<sp/>by<sp/>using<sp/>a<sp/>substitution<sp/>of<sp/>variables.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">The<sp/>state<sp/>vector<sp/>of<sp/>the<sp/>agent<sp/>then<sp/>goes<sp/>from<sp/>having<sp/>one<sp/>element<sp/>to<sp/>\f$n\f$<sp/>elements,<sp/>where<sp/>the<sp/>derivative<sp/>of<sp/>the<sp/>\f$i^{th}\f$<sp/>component<sp/>is<sp/>used<sp/>to<sp/>compute<sp/>the<sp/>derivative<sp/>of<sp/>the<sp/>\f$(i+1)^{th}\f$<sp/>component.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">This<sp/>process<sp/>is<sp/>further<sp/>detailed<sp/>in<sp/>the<sp/>@ref<sp/>highorder<sp/>&quot;Higher-Order<sp/>Dynamics&quot;<sp/>examples.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">##<sp/>Dynamic<sp/>Topologies<sp/>{#dyntop}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">The<sp/>size,<sp/>order,<sp/>and<sp/>topology<sp/>are<sp/>usually<sp/>fixed<sp/>for<sp/>a<sp/>given<sp/>network<sp/>i.e.,<sp/>once<sp/>the<sp/>network<sp/>is<sp/>created,<sp/>these<sp/>variables<sp/>cannot<sp/>-<sp/>and<sp/>do<sp/>not<sp/>-<sp/>change.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">For<sp/>some<sp/>applications<sp/>and<sp/>models,<sp/>this<sp/>approach<sp/>is<sp/>sufficient.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">However,<sp/>there<sp/>also<sp/>exist<sp/>networks<sp/>for<sp/>which<sp/>these<sp/>variables<sp/>are<sp/>not<sp/>constant<sp/>(see<sp/>the<sp/>examples<sp/>listed<sp/>in<sp/>the<sp/>@ref<sp/>introduction);<sp/>in<sp/>these<sp/>cases,<sp/>&quot;dead&quot;<sp/>agents<sp/>are<sp/>usually<sp/>simulated<sp/>by<sp/>zeroing<sp/>their<sp/>contributions<sp/>to<sp/>the<sp/>overall<sp/>dynamics,<sp/>and<sp/>&quot;new&quot;<sp/>agents<sp/>are<sp/>simulated<sp/>by<sp/>reserving<sp/>space<sp/>before<sp/>the<sp/>simulation<sp/>for<sp/>their<sp/>eventual<sp/>existence.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">This<sp/>wastes<sp/>computational<sp/>resources,<sp/>and<sp/>also<sp/>provides<sp/>a<sp/>hard<sp/>limit<sp/>on<sp/>the<sp/>amount<sp/>of<sp/>new<sp/>agents<sp/>that<sp/>can<sp/>be<sp/>brought<sp/>into<sp/>the<sp/>network.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">Simulating<sp/>these<sp/>kinds<sp/>of<sp/>networks<sp/>is<sp/>specifically<sp/>what<sp/>NDXL<sp/>was<sp/>designed<sp/>for:<sp/>by<sp/>allowing<sp/>agents<sp/>to<sp/>be<sp/>created<sp/>and<sp/>destroyed<sp/>during<sp/>simulation,<sp/>only<sp/>ever<sp/>those<sp/>that<sp/>are<sp/>still<sp/>part<sp/>of<sp/>the<sp/>network<sp/>are<sp/>actually<sp/>simulated.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">See<sp/>@ref<sp/>dynnet<sp/>for<sp/>details<sp/>how<sp/>to<sp/>simulate<sp/>dynamic<sp/>topology<sp/>networks,<sp/>what<sp/>the<sp/>rules<sp/>are<sp/>for<sp/>when<sp/>and<sp/>how<sp/>to<sp/>add/remove/rearrange<sp/>agents,<sp/>and<sp/>what<sp/>the<sp/>limitations,<sp/>mathematical<sp/>implications,<sp/>and<sp/>performance<sp/>impacts<sp/>are.</highlight></codeline>
    </programlisting>
